# Tallyvis environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (for apps/web / apps/app) and fill in real values.
# NEVER commit a file containing real secrets — only .env.example is tracked in git.
#
# Most of what's below is not consumed by the codebase yet. Each block is
# reserved for the phase that introduces it, so the shape of future
# configuration is visible now.

# --- Phase 4: cross-app links (apps/web <-> apps/app) ---
# Both have working defaults for local dev (localhost:3000 / :3001) — only
# set these when deploying somewhere real.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3001
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MARKETING_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Phase 9: services/api database ---
# Where services/api's SQLite file lives. Optional for local development —
# unset defaults to services/api/data/tallyvis.dev.db (gitignored), created
# automatically on first use. Set to ":memory:" for an ephemeral database,
# or a real file path when deploying somewhere with persistent disk. This
# is read by whichever Node process imports @tallyvis/api (apps/app's
# Next.js server), so set it in apps/app/.env.local, not here, for local
# overrides. See docs/decisions/0011-persistence-auth-and-multi-tenancy.md.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Phase 9 authentication has no secret to configure — sessions are opaque
# random tokens hashed at rest (see the ADR above), not signed JWTs, so
# there's no signing key to rotate or leak.

# --- Phase 11: AI property analysis (services/ai, orchestrated by
# services/api — apps/app never calls a provider or sees this key) ---
# AI_PROVIDER selects which provider services/ai uses: "mock" (default when
# unset — the same deterministic heuristic the estimator has used since
# Phase 4, no key needed) or "anthropic" (Claude, via @anthropic-ai/sdk;
# requires AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY below). See
# docs/decisions/0013-ai-analysis-foundation.md.
# AI_PROVIDER=mock
#
# Only read when AI_PROVIDER=anthropic. Server-side only — read exclusively
# inside services/ai/src/providers/anthropic.ts, never bundled to the
# browser, never logged, never returned from any Server Action. Get a key
# from https://console.anthropic.com/ if you want to try the real provider
# locally; leave this unset to keep using the mock.
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
#
# Optional — which Claude model to use. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5 if unset.
# AI_PROVIDER_MODEL=

# --- Phase 14: notifications (services/api, orchestrated server-side —
# apps/app never calls a provider or sees these credentials) ---
# EMAIL_PROVIDER selects which provider services/api/notifications uses:
# "dev" (default when unset — logs the full message, including any link,
# to the server console; never a real send) or "resend" (real transactional
# email via Resend's HTTP API; requires RESEND_API_KEY and
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS below). See
# docs/decisions/0016-onboarding-billing-embed.md.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=dev
#
# Only read when EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend. Server-side only — read exclusively
# inside services/api/notifications/providers/resend.ts, never bundled to
# the browser, never logged. Get a key from https://resend.com/ if you
# want to try real delivery locally; leave unset to keep using the dev
# provider.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=

# --- Phase 14: billing (Stripe) — see docs/decisions/0018-stripe-v1-hardening.md ---
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY selects real billing — unset means checkout is
# unavailable and the dashboard says so honestly. Server-side only — read
# exclusively inside services/api/billing/index.ts. NEVER commit a real
# value; use a TEST-MODE secret key (starts sk_test_...) for local
# development, a LIVE-MODE key (sk_live_...) only in a real production
# deployment, and never mix the two.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
#
# Verifies the signature on incoming Stripe webhook events
# (apps/app/src/app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts). Unset means that
# endpoint responds 501 rather than processing anything unverified. Each
# Stripe webhook endpoint (test-mode and live-mode are configured
# separately in the Stripe Dashboard) has its own signing secret
# (whsec_...) — use the one for the webhook endpoint pointed at THIS
# environment.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
#
# Persistent Stripe Price ids for the three recurring plans and the
# one-time professional installation fee (see @tallyvis/config's PLANS and
# PROFESSIONAL_INSTALLATION_FEE, and services/api/src/billing/index.ts's
# resolveStripePriceId/resolveInstallationPriceId — the only place these
# are read). NOT secrets, but still environment-specific: a test-mode
# Stripe account and a live-mode Stripe account issue DIFFERENT ids for
# "the same" price, so these must point at test-mode ids in local
# dev/CI/Vercel preview, and live-mode ids only in production — never
# left over from the other mode.
# STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=
# STRIPE_PRICE_GROWTH=
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=
# STRIPE_PRICE_INSTALLATION=

# --- V1 account features: Google Sign-In (see
# docs/decisions/0019-account-settings-and-google-auth.md) ---
# Both unset means the "Continue with Google" buttons safely no-op
# (redirect back with a "not configured" message) rather than erroring.
# Read directly in apps/app's Google OAuth route handlers
# (apps/app/src/app/api/auth/google/{start,callback}/route.ts) — never
# bundled to the browser, never logged. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID
# (type: Web application) at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials,
# with an Authorized redirect URI of
# `${NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL}/api/auth/google/callback` (e.g.
# http://localhost:3001/api/auth/google/callback for local dev).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- General ---
# NODE_ENV=development
